Notes from the repro:
- It's a little odd to use StreamContent on the server, I'd have expected a StreamReader instead. Shouldn't hurt anything though.
- Nothing else stands out as an obvious cause of this.

> Sending API ->(HTTP/2)-> F5 VIP --> F5 Server Side ->(HTTP/2)-> Receiving API - Does Not Work
> Sending API ->(HTTP/1.1)-> F5 VIP --> F5 Server Side ->(HTTP/2)-> Receiving API - Works OK

The fact that it works when you change the client to use HTTP/1.1 to F5 implies an issue with the HttpClient, not the ASP.NET Server in the receiving API.

Next steps:
- Are you able to repro this using .NET 5? There were a lot of HTTP/2 improvements in 5.
- Have you found any way to reproduce this without the F5 component? We don't have one of those 😁. 
- What if you tested this combo? Sending API ->(HTTP/2)-> F5 VIP --> F5 Server Side ->(HTTP/1.1)-> Receiving API 

>I do have wireshark traces that I have sent to F5 and can easily reproduce the issue.

Are they decrypted? Encrypted traces aren't going to help here.

To rule out any issues on the server side you can also collect debug level logs from the receiving API, including decrypted wire content using the connection logging component in Kestrel: https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/core/fundamentals/servers/kestrel/endpoints?view=aspnetcore-5.0#connection-logging
```c#
webBuilder.ConfigureKestrel(serverOptions =>
{
    serverOptions.Listen(IPAddress.Any, 8000, listenOptions =>
    {
        listenOptions.UseHttps();
        listenOptions.UseConnectionLogging();
    });
});
```
https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/core/fundamentals/logging/?view=aspnetcore-5.0#configure-logging

If we don't see any obvious issues on the server side then I'll transfer you to https://github.com/dotnet/runtime for more HttpClient help.

Given the above (the fact F5 uses something that leads to more problems), I wonder if we should backport our fix or not.
@deathchurch how much is it blocking you? If the fix is only in 6.0, are you able to consume it and use it to unblock yourself?

If we have more customers hitting it, I am all for backporting.
